From: hawkff <109485367+hawkff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:53:42 +0000
Subject: Destroy the incognito profile after its tab model

When the last incognito tab is closed, IncognitoTabModelImpl notifies its
IncognitoTabModelObservers and then destroys its delegate tab model. One of
these observers, IncognitoProfileDestroyer, asked for the incognito profile
to be destroyed during that notification, and when no renderer process of
that profile was left, the profile was deleted right away. The delegate
TabCollectionTabModelImpl and its native objects were destroyed only after
that, while they still pointed at the deleted profile: the native
TabCollectionTabModelImpl holds a raw_ptr<Profile>. With dangling pointer
detection in crash mode, this can end the browser process.

IncognitoTabModelObserver gets onEmptyModelDestroyed(), which
IncognitoTabModelImpl calls after it has destroyed the emptied tab model and
replaced it with the empty stub. IncognitoProfileDestroyer decides in
didBecomeEmpty() as before, but destroys the profile in
onEmptyModelDestroyed(), in the same call stack. The existing notifications
and the tab model teardown keep their order, and nothing is deferred to a
later task, so no new incognito tab can start on the old profile in between.

